# Citation metadata of the UWB-ASC testing ground. The release date and both
# DOIs were filled on 2026-11-08 from the DOIs reserved on Zenodo, before the
# first version was published. The preferred citation, the preprint of the
# data descriptor, was added on 2026-11-10 after its arXiv announcement.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or this code, please cite the data descriptor (preferred-citation) and the dataset by its DOI."
type: dataset
title: "UWB Anchor Self-Calibration Dataset (UWB-ASC)"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-08"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24055896"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24055896"
    description: "The version DOI of version 1.0.0 on Zenodo."
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24055895"
    description: "The concept DOI of all versions on Zenodo, which resolves to the latest version."
abstract: >-
  A testing ground for the self-calibration of UWB anchor positions: two
  deployments of Qorvo MDEK1001 modules in one industrial hall in Torgau,
  Germany, with surveyed node positions, motion-capture truth for the walks of
  the LOS deployment and surveyed markers for the NLOS deployment, a seeded
  range-error generator as code with frozen synthetic draws on the surveyed
  geometry and a tool that draws new scenes, the canonical measurement graph
  with four topology views, the raw recordings with the scripts that rebuild
  the canonical files, and readers for two public range recordings.
authors:
  - family-names: "Schwarzbach"
    given-names: "Paul"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1091-782X"
    affiliation: "TUD Dresden University of Technology"
# The data and the documentation are under CC BY 4.0 and the code under MIT (README.md,
# "Licences"). CFF reads a list of licences as alternatives (OR), which would offer the
# data under MIT, so only the licence of the cited dataset stands here.
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
